ay is the vac banned  account now there's not a lot of  information on it but just look at some  of the past names mad hacker leet mad  cos bad why you bad  get rekt get rekt mate suka blat blat  suka mean come on that's not a cheater  account I don't know what is now I know  what you're saying call him  why should a young Pro with a vac banned  account even be given a second chance  what right does he have to sue valve  well according to yam P it all started  back in 2015 when he was 14 years old a  young yam P and his buddies were having  a  and party at yam peas house now not  everybody on csgo so he took his parents  credit card with permission I assume  bought a bunch of copies and started  handing them out now at least one of  those friends pays him back that night  for the game thus in some way  transferring ownership of that account  from yam pea to his buddy no remember  that because that's gonna be important  later now eventually this buddies  account the one that yam P originally  bought for him and that he payed for  allegedly gets a vac ban now we don't  know exactly why or exactly what this  guy did with his account but according  to a letter that's entered into evidence  in this lawsuit the guy installed cheats  in order to beat another friend at a 1v1  game now remember this account was  created by yam P so it's still  associated with his identity flash  forward to 2019 and yam P is given his  big first contract with og eSports I  mean look this was a rare opportunity  for yam he's a young csgo player at the  start of his career and in comes this  big legacy organization like og wanna  put their first foot in csgo and they're  offering big money for it  you gotta believe this was a dream come  true for the guy only problem was that  the contractual negotiations fell apart  when the team learned that yappi was  associated with a vac banned account now  according to the lawsuit when yam P  found out there was a vac banned account  associated with his name apparently he  didn't know up until now he contacted  valve believe it or not they exchanged  emails stories were told proof was  offered but valve would not budge and  the young finn remain banned valves  responses were short simple and brutally  clear like this one hi Elias we received  a question below about your eligibility  to play in majors our investigation has  found a vac banned account that we've  concluded was under your control at the  time of the band therefore you are not  eligible to participate at our events  best of luck to you but yeah he kept  trying he lawyered up and at one point  even invoked the European data  protection regulation but valve still  wouldn't budge his team SJ gaming also  reached out and so did the  counter-strike Players Association but  neither had any more luck than yam pian  self and so here we are sitting at a  forty page lawsuit so what's filling the  forty pages well aside from telling his  story and offering proof for the whole  2015 LAN party thing the MP also invokes  the Finnish Consumer Protection Act  which among other things states the  following if a term in a contract  referred to in the act is unreasonable  for the point of view of the consumer or  if an unreasonable result would ensue  from its application the term may be  adjusted or it may be disregarded  basically what yam pees lawsuit is  arguing is that when he was 14 years old  and he bought those counter strike  accounts he was a consumer buying a  product and having his entire pro career  limited so severely by a vac ban on  account that he allegedly denieth in  control is unreasonable and therefore  should be disregarded the lawsuit also  emphasizes that as a child a 14-year old  cannot quote take into account the  impact of a lifelong ban other  prohibition or punishment in their  future life and they also say that the  Steam User Agreement doesn't say  anything about not attending majors even  if you have a vac ban now from Valve's  point of view there is a section on the  steam website under frequently asked  questions that does seem to address this  sort of thing it's under the header I  was not using my account when it was vac  banned can the ban be removed and the  answer is quote no regardless of who was  using the account at the time of the  infraction vac bans are permanent and  will not be removed while we understand  this can be frustrating we must maintain  a zero-tolerance policy for cheating to  foster a fair game that all players will  enjoy and from the emails that are  offered into evidence for this lawsuit  it doesn't seem like gaben &amp; Co are  changing their minds on this any time  soon  I read you one email from valve earlier  and there are several others but they  all basically say the same thing they're  short curt to the point and the gist of  it is sorry kid best of luck now at the  risk of editorializing a little bit this  all just seems kind of unfair doesn't it  I mean if we believe the story about yam  P not being involved with the back ban  at all and at this point it is still  alleged then it seems like  that we're never gonna see this guy play  csgo at the highest level he's obviously  a player with some merit or else oh gee  wouldn't be so eager to have signed him  at this point we're never gonna see what  he can really do at a top level and it  seems like he might not have done  anything wrong to deserve that  there are several letters entered into  evidence in this lawsuit that seemed to  be written by yam P himself and in them  he comes off really honest and really  sincere  guys this kid just wants to play CS he  wants to live the eSports dream and he's  willing to suffer an investigation to  prove what he's saying is true if valve  can just step up do their part and clear  his name then he can get on with doing  what he loves to do and we can watch him  do it alright guys I got the emails I  got the comments I got the Twitter DM I  know you're all very upset that my Ga